WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.466
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.766 --> 00:00:09.280
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:15.008
Unit eleven: There is / There are. Today you will say what exists in a place.

4
00:00:15.308 --> 00:00:17.879
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:22.078
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:23.778
There is.

7
00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:27.607
There is means used to say that one thing exists.

8
00:00:28.217 --> 00:00:29.682
There is a cat in the garden.

9
00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:32.820
Your turn. Say: There is.

10
00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:36.772
There is.

11
00:00:37.517 --> 00:00:38.471
There are.

12
00:00:39.483 --> 00:00:41.970
There are means used to say that many things exist.

13
00:00:42.583 --> 00:00:44.339
There are two books on the table.

14
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:48.183
Your turn. Say: There are.

15
00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:51.988
There are.

16
00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:53.647
A cat.

17
00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:56.220
A cat means one cat.

18
00:00:56.817 --> 00:00:58.294
A cat is on the chair.

19
00:00:58.883 --> 00:01:02.000
Your turn. Say: A cat.

20
00:01:04.867 --> 00:01:05.717
A cat.

21
00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:07.635
Some books.

22
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:11.242
Some books means an unknown number of books.

23
00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.176
Some books are new.

24
00:01:13.783 --> 00:01:16.482
Your turn. Say: Some books.

25
00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:20.474
Some books.

26
00:01:21.217 --> 00:01:22.357
Existence.

27
00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:27.079
Existence means the fact that something is real or is there.

28
00:01:27.683 --> 00:01:30.287
Existence is the idea behind there is.

29
00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:33.675
Your turn. Say: Existence.

30
00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:37.790
Existence.

31
00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:39.748
Singular noun.

32
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:43.400
Singular noun means a noun that means one thing.

33
00:01:43.983 --> 00:01:45.704
Book is a singular noun.

34
00:01:46.317 --> 00:01:48.911
Your turn. Say: Singular noun.

35
00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:53.162
Singular noun.

36
00:01:53.917 --> 00:01:54.918
Plural noun.

37
00:01:55.917 --> 00:01:58.741
Plural noun means a noun that means more than one thing.

38
00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:01.013
Books is a plural noun.

39
00:02:01.617 --> 00:02:04.397
Your turn. Say: Plural noun.

40
00:02:07.233 --> 00:02:08.525
Plural noun.

41
00:02:09.283 --> 00:02:10.308
Location.

42
00:02:11.317 --> 00:02:13.699
Location means the place where something is.

43
00:02:14.283 --> 00:02:16.225
The location is the classroom.

44
00:02:16.817 --> 00:02:19.399
Your turn. Say: Location.

45
00:02:22.233 --> 00:02:23.362
Location.

46
00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:27.632
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.483 --> 00:02:31.937
Visal, look at the classroom. What can you say about it?

48
00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:40.520
There is a board, and there are many chairs. We use there is with a singular noun and there are with a plural noun.

49
00:02:41.617 --> 00:02:43.094
How do we make a negative?

50
00:02:44.183 --> 00:02:51.030
Add not: There is not a clock. There are not any windows. In speaking we say there isn't and there aren't.

51
00:02:52.117 --> 00:02:53.385
And questions?

52
00:02:54.483 --> 00:03:03.654
We change the order: Is there a library? Are there any students? We often answer: Yes, there is. No, there aren't.

53
00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.533
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:07.383 --> 00:03:10.114
Grammar focus: There is and There are.

55
00:03:10.414 --> 00:03:11.624
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:12.317 --> 00:03:13.887
There is a cat in the garden.

57
00:03:14.783 --> 00:03:16.678
There are three books on the table.

58
00:03:17.583 --> 00:03:19.211
There isn't a clock in the room.

59
00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:28.371
Use there is with a singular noun and there are with a plural noun. Use there isn't and there aren't for negatives. Questions: Is there…? Are there…?

60
00:03:29.117 --> 00:03:32.431
Be careful! Don't say: There is two pens.

61
00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:36.389
Say: There are two pens.

62
00:03:36.689 --> 00:03:38.596
Use there are with a plural noun.

63
00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.145
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:42.933 --> 00:03:44.097
My Classroom.

65
00:03:44.397 --> 00:03:46.466
There is a big board in my classroom.

66
00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:50.569
There are thirty chairs, and there are some posters on the wall.

67
00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:54.332
There is a window, but there isn't a clock.

68
00:03:55.333 --> 00:03:57.286
Is there a library in your school?

69
00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.926
Yes, there is, and there are many books in it.

70
00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:06.221
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:07.083 --> 00:04:08.700
blank a cat in the garden.

72
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.328
A, There is. B, There are. C, They are.

73
00:04:15.867 --> 00:04:17.808
The answer is A: There is.

74
00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.810
blank five books on the shelf.

75
00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:24.241
A, There is. B, There are. C, It is.

76
00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.544
The answer is B: There are.

77
00:04:30.683 --> 00:04:32.532
blank any students in the room?

78
00:04:32.832 --> 00:04:36.590
A, Is there. B, Are there. C, There are.

79
00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:42.110
The answer is B: Are there.

80
00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:45.041
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:45.341 --> 00:04:50.631
A, There is two pens.. B, There are two pens.. C, There be two pens..

82
00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:56.816
The answer is B: There are two pens..

83
00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:00.298
According to the reading, what is there on the wall?

84
00:05:00.598 --> 00:05:05.308
A, a clock. B, some posters. C, a library.

85
00:05:08.867 --> 00:05:11.156
The answer is B: some posters.

86
00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:15.518
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:16.383 --> 00:05:19.103
Describe your classroom using 'there is' and 'there are'.

88
00:05:27.917 --> 00:05:29.545
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:29.845 --> 00:05:42.229
There is a big board in my classroom, and there are many chairs and tables. There is a map on the wall, and there are some posters too. I use there is for one thing and there are for many things.

90
00:05:42.529 --> 00:05:44.319
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:45.217 --> 00:05:49.390
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and there is and there are.

92
00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:53.782
Today's value is gratitude. Say thank you for your home and family.

93
00:05:54.082 --> 00:05:56.827
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

94
00:05:57.127 --> 00:06:00.139
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

